From ab5f3103a9b4338e92cb782f4fc861aa5f497b02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:20:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] health: drop the health@2.0 service

error: hardware/waydroid/health/Android.bp:16:1:
"android.hardware.health@2.0-service.waydroid" depends on undefined module
"android.hardware.health@2.0-impl".

Android 15 dropped health 2.0's default impl and made 2.1 binderized, so
libhealthservice and health2/service.h are gone. This service cannot build.

Nothing references it. device.mk lists android.hardware.health-service.example
instead, AOSP's own fake-battery service, which is also what lineage-23.2 uses.
Soong builds this dead module and gains nothing from it.
---
 health/Android.bp                             | 50 ----------------
 ...id.hardware.health@2.0-service.waydroid.rc |  4 --
 health/health_service.cpp                     | 57 -------------------
 3 files changed, 111 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 health/Android.bp
 delete mode 100644 health/android.hardware.health@2.0-service.waydroid.rc
 delete mode 100644 health/health_service.cpp

diff --git a/health/Android.bp b/health/Android.bp
deleted file mode 100644
index b5cee78..0000000
